Case Study 1: Traffic Violation Penalty Calculator
1. Problem Statement
Calculate fines for multiple traffic violations using vehicle category, offence type, and repeat-offence status. Identify whether disqualification review is needed.

2. Objectives
•	Read multiple violation records.
•	Apply sample fines and the repeat-offence rule.
•	Calculate the total penalty and review status.

3. Assumptions
•	Sample fines: helmet = ₹500, signal = ₹1000, speeding = ₹1500.
•	A repeat offence doubles its fine.
•	Three or more violations require disqualification review.

4. Algorithm
1. Start.
2. Read the number of violations.
3. For each violation, read vehicle, offence and repeat status; calculate its fine.
4. Add each fine to the total.
5. If violations are 3 or more, show review required; otherwise show no review flag.
6. Display total and stop.

5. Flowchart
Oval = Start/End; Parallelogram = Input/Output; Rectangle = Process; Diamond = Decision.
